==Rules==
{{ColosseumRule|Cheap Labor}}

==Battleground==
*6 [[Zroco]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 40~43.33 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Cerberus Kids]] spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
*1 [[Zyclone]] spawns after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Hannya]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[Zapy]] spawns after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
**2 [[Devil Wife|Devil Wives]] spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 53.33~56.67 seconds<sup>1,600f~1,700f</sup>.
**2 [[Cadaver Bear]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 60~63.33 seconds<sup>1,800f~1,900f</sup>.
**1 [[Zyclone]] spawns after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
It's easy to think that the combination of Hannya, Zyclone, and Cadaver Bear would make this stage almost impossible, but it's surprisingly very simple. Most enemies lack sustained pushing power, and similarly to the first stage, you can somewhat reliably keep them in place with [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]], [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]] and [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] aided by a Defense Up [[Cat Combo]]. [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] and [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] can deal with the peons, so focus on opening up a clear path for [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]] to land solid hits on Zapy and eventually Zyclone. You want [[Ototo Corps#Holy Blast|Holy Blast]] to unburrow the two Cadaver Bears when they spawn, otherwise they lose you plenty of ground that you cannot easily regain. It doesn't really matter whether you Z-Kill them, since they hardly pose a threat with the meager support they're provided, but just try to prevent them from stacking up if you can. Another tip is to let [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] hit the enemy base, since this allows him to burst down over half of Hannya's HP.

